 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Usage reporting across tool rounds
+
+`afterModelResponse` receives the aggregated provider-call usage for the entire turn, so a deployer's billing, audit, or budget accounting includes every leg of a multi-round turn. The aggregation is captured in `UsageMetadata` — its token fields sum only provider calls that reported usage, and a turn in which no provider call reported usage reports `undefined`, exactly as a single-round turn with no reported usage does.
+
+- The aggregation function `aggregateUsage` sums token counts from multiple provider call results ([validated by: sums usage from multiple rounds](../../src/orchestration/aggregateUsage.test.ts#L5)).
+- When no provider call in a turn reports usage, aggregation returns `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when no rounds report usage](../../src/orchestration/aggregateUsage.test.ts#L17)).
+- The aggregation function skips undefined round results and sums only those that reported usage ([validated by: sums only rounds that report usage, ignoring undefined](../../src/orchestration/aggregateUsage.test.ts#L23)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what it reports today ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+- A turn with multiple provider calls reports the sum of every call's reported tokens ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+- Missing round usage does not poison reported totals, and an entirely unreported turn remains undefined ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
